            <ArticleTitle>Endovascular stenting of an unprotected left main coronary artery stenosis in a heart transplant patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>919-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Endoluminal revascularizaion of left main coronary artery vessels is considered to be relatively contraindicated because of a high procedural mortality and restenosis rate. This report describes the first successful case of endovascular stenting in an unprotected left main coronary artery stenosis in a heart transplant patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
